---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="check" first="done" title="Make it prove it" description="An agent reports done whether or not the work is right. Automated checks between the agent and you bounce broken work straight back.">
  <Step id="done" title="It says “done” either way">
    <p>Run six example tasks through <a href={url('journey/loop/')}>the agent loop</a>. Three come out broken (shown in orange), yet all six arrive on your desk marked “done”.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="tests" title="Put an automated check in the way">
    <ForLevel is="plain">
      <p>Put a check between the agent and you. Whenever something breaks, the check bounces it straight back to the agent to fix before you ever have to look.</p>
      <More title="A prompt for this">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Ask for proof with the work">{`Before you tell me it is done:\n1. Run the project's checks and paste the result.\n2. Open the page at phone width, take a screenshot and confirm nothing overflows.\n3. Tell me what I should click to try it myself.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="technical">
      <p>Wire <code>tsc --noEmit</code> and automated unit tests (<code>vitest run</code> / <code>pytest</code>) as a mandatory gate. Broken types or failing assertions bounce straight back into the loop automatically.</p>
      <More title="A prompt for this">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Verification gate prompt">{`Before reporting done:\n1. Run tsc --noEmit and the full unit test suite; paste the final summary line.\n2. Add a regression unit test covering the change or bug fix.\n3. If UI changed, inspect a 390 px and 1280 px screenshot and fix any overflow.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="engineer">
      <p>Treat verification as a first-class architectural asset: fast strict typechecking, deterministic unit/integration suites and headless browser checks turn open-ended generation into a self-correcting inner loop.</p>
      <More title="A prompt for this">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Contract-level verification prompt">{`Do not report completion until:\n1. Strict typecheck, lint and unit/integration suites are all green (include command output).\n2. New invariants and boundary cases have deterministic unit tests.\n3. Any UI surface passes headless viewport checks (390 px + desktop) with zero console errors.\n4. List any assumptions or gaps automated checks did not cover.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
  </Step>
  <Step id="more" title="Each check catches a different kind of miss">
    <p>Now three checks stand between the agent and you. Turn any one off and watch which bug slips right through:</p>
    <div class="pick" data-multi role="group" aria-label="Checks that are switched on">
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="tests" data-default aria-pressed="true">Types &amp; unit tests</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="look" data-default aria-pressed="true">Browser screenshot</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="review" data-default aria-pressed="true">Second model</button>
    </div>
    <More title="What each layer catches">
      <dl class="j-defs">
        <dt>Types &amp; unit tests</dt><dd>Fast commands (<code>tsc --noEmit</code>, unit suite) that prove logic, edge cases and type contracts.</dd>
        <dt>Browser screenshot</dt><dd>Opens the rendered page at phone and desktop widths to catch broken layouts and overlap.</dd>
        <dt>Second model</dt><dd>A fresh model reads only the brief and diff to catch privacy leaks, missed rules and architectural flaws.</dd>
      </dl>
    </More>
    <Next from="check" more={[{ href: 'wiki/verification/', text: 'Verification', side: true }, { href: 'journey/proof/', text: 'Proof you can read (step 16)' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The six tasks and failure types above are illustrative examples.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
